WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.283
Durability mechanisms matter only with a workable
recovery path.

00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:09.570
Several persistence layers helped retain data, but
queues have finite capacity.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.511
Backups need tested restores.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:16.329
Startup dependencies can form cycles that require a
bootstrap mechanism.

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:21.482
Rehearse a cold recovery so the first attempt is not
under incident pressure.

00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:26.769
Do not mistake an accidental unupgraded component
for a sound upgrade strategy.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.331
Recovery should restore customer value.

00:00:29.331 --> 00:00:33.550
A system with a backlog needs spare capacity beyond
new arrivals.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:39.976
At one hundred arrivals per second and one hundred
twenty completions per second, only twenty items

00:00:39.976 --> 00:00:41.664
per second drain old work.

00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:45.623
Prioritize urgent traffic and throttle backfill
deliberately.

00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:51.984
Practice degraded operation and retain independent
visibility when the main monitoring path fails.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.415
The final discussion connects AI-assisted
development to quality.

00:00:56.415 --> 00:01:01.712
Generating code quickly does not prove that a team
can maintain or operate it.

00:01:01.712 --> 00:01:08.504
For a lasting service, define security, reliability
and change scenarios, inspect the implementation

00:01:08.504 --> 00:01:09.930
and collect evidence.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:15.228
A successful demo is one observation, not a complete
architectural evaluation.
